WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.340
I was in Philadelphia for a conference when I saw an ad in the hotel.
我到费城开会时，在酒店里看到了一则广告。

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:14.460
A nearby theater was showing a documentary about several local animal shelters that were helping to save abandoned dogs across the country.
附近一家剧院正在放映一部纪录片，讲的是当地几家动物收容所如何帮忙救助全国各地被遗弃的狗。

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:19.320
I love animals, and I felt an urge to go to this fundraising event.
我很喜欢动物，心里涌起一股冲动，想去参加这场募捐活动。

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:25.790
However, none of my co-workers would go with me, and I was worried about walking on the street alone at night.
然而，同事们谁也不愿意陪我去，而我又担心晚上独自走在街上不安全。

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:33.550
I resigned myself to spending the evening in my hotel room, but as soon as I got back to my room I felt restless and bored.
我只好认命，打算在酒店房间里度过这个夜晚，可是一回到房间，我就感到坐立不安、百无聊赖。

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:43.260
The theater where the event was taking place was only about five blocks from the hotel, and the area around the hotel didn’t seem particularly dangerous.
举办活动的剧院离酒店只有大约五个街区，而且酒店周围看起来也不是特别危险。

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.680
So, I decided to brave it.
于是，我决定壮着胆子去一趟。

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.010
I gathered up my wallet and room key and set off.
我收拾好钱包和房卡，就出发了。

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:53.060
It was already getting dark and the streets were nearly deserted.
天已经渐渐黑了，街上几乎空无一人。

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.420
I managed to find the street the theater was on, but when I turned the corner, I stopped in shock.
我总算找到了剧院所在的那条街，可是一拐过街角，我就惊呆了，停下了脚步。

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.760
In front of the theater were a group of bikers—very big, tough-looking bikers.
剧院门前站着一群机车骑手——个个人高马大，看上去凶悍得很。

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.510
I’ve known lots of motorcycle enthusiasts and most are nice people.
我认识不少摩托车爱好者，他们大多是好人。

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:23.620
However, in this case, I was a woman all alone, in a strange neighborhood, at night, and there were twenty or so very large men—all wearing insignia that indicated they were in some sort of club—standing before me.
然而这一次，我是一个女人，孤零零的，身处陌生的街区，又是晚上，而面前站着二十来个人高马大的男人——个个都佩戴着徽章，表明他们属于某个俱乐部。

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.230
Warning bells began to sound in my head, and my heart was pounding.
我脑子里警铃大作，心怦怦直跳。

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:30.380
Was I at the right theater?
我是不是走错剧院了？

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.980
Had I misread the date of the event?
难道我看错了活动日期？

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.220
A sign outside the theater told me that I was in the right place on the right evening.
剧院外的一块告示牌告诉我，地方没错，日子也没错。

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:45.080
Nevertheless, I wondered if I should rush back to my hotel instead of walking through that crowd of bikers.
尽管如此，我还是犹豫要不要赶紧跑回酒店，免得从那群骑手中间穿过去。

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.200
I finally decided that I would be safer inside the theater.
最后，我认定待在剧院里面会更安全些。

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.620
Hopefully, the bikers would have gone away by the time the film was over.
但愿等电影放完，那些骑手已经走了。

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.930
I hurried into the theater, only to find there were even more bikers inside.
我匆匆走进剧院，没想到里面的骑手更多。

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:04.190
When the film began, I realized that the bikers were an animal rescue group.
电影开始后，我才意识到这些骑手是一个动物救助团体。
